# Delete a step from the development flow

Deleting a step removes its state from `.df/<flow>/flow.json`, deletes its directory
`.df/<flow>/steps/<step-id>/` (template and any extra files) and uninstalls its skill from every
configured coding agent. Transitions that pointed to the step are rewired so the flow stays
connected, and a transition that would then point back at its own step is removed. This is
destructive, so explain the consequences and get explicit confirmation first.

